    "finding": "The strict live linkcheck passes on candidate and main, but the candidate incurred six Sphinx rate-limit waits and took about 252 seconds while the main check incurred two waits and took about 133 seconds. The 429s are on existing GitHub UI links; retries and strict failure behavior completed normally. CI invokes one full CI workflow per PR event and one per main push; Docs Deploy is a separate HTML deployment, so no duplicate strict linkcheck was found. Caching, ignored URLs, or reducing retries would weaken live acceptance. One-worker mode was previously observed to be slower. Sphinx documents a default of five workers, so a bounded two-worker experiment is selected to measure whether lower request concurrency reduces rate-limit waits without changing URL coverage, retries, backoff, or strict success requirements.",
    "next_experiment": {
      "change": "Set linkcheck_workers=2 in docs/conf.py for one exact-candidate trial.",
      "preserve": [
        "all current URLs",
        "sphinx-build -b linkcheck -W",
        "default retries",
        "default Retry-After/backoff",
        "warning-as-failure semantics"
      ],
      "acceptance": "Compare strict candidate linkcheck duration and rate-limit counts to the measured default-five-worker runs; retain the setting only if full validation still passes and measured latency improves."
